---
source: crates/jailint/tests/rules.rs
---
warning[pointer_into_resizable]: `first` points into `items`, which `array_add` may have moved by now
  --> tests/lint/pointer_into_resizable/bad.jai:23:12
   |
18 |     first := *items[0];
   |              --------- pointer derived here
   ...
20 |     array_add(*items, .{ 2 });
   |     ------------------------- `items` storage invalidated here
   ...
23 |     return first.value;
   |            ^^^^^ pointer used here after its storage was invalidated
   |
   = help: take the pointer again after the array has grown, or keep the index instead
   = note: `pointer_into_resizable` is `warn` by default
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/pointer_into_resizable

warning[pointer_into_resizable]: `slot` points into `storage.items`, which `array_reserve` may have moved by now
  --> tests/lint/pointer_into_resizable/bad.jai:30:12
   |
27 |     slot := *store.items[0].value;
   |             --------------------- pointer derived here
28 |     array_reserve(*store.items, 1000);
   |     --------------------------------- `storage.items` storage invalidated here
   ...
30 |     return slot.*;
   |            ^^^^ pointer used here after its storage was invalidated
   |
  ::: [repo]/stdlib/internal/basic/arrays.jai:19:5
   |
19 |     array_reserve(cast(*Resizable_Array) array, desired_items, size_of(T));
   |     ---------------------------------------------------------------------- invalidation inferred through this call
   |
   = help: take the pointer again after the array has grown, or keep the index instead
   = note: `pointer_into_resizable` is `warn` by default
   = note: see https://jacket.matteopolak.com/lint-rules/pointer_into_resizable

